The `oid.value` array has a fixed size of `SC_MAX_OBJECT_ID_OCTETS` (16). The loop copies `blob->len - 1` bytes from `blob->data[1]` into `oid.value[]`, but there's no bounds check. If `blob->len > 17`, this will write past the end of the `oid.value[16]` array, causing a stack-buffer-overflow.

